From 0e3ca4283cf82456875f58df3e5e4e22bc413835 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Corios00 <52224974+Corios00@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:08:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] The client's guards pay down what the tests patch loosened

Patch 0094 raised the world API wall's ceiling, exempted four look passes from the warm-pass
test and raised the schedule ceilings. This takes back what can be taken back without changing
play or looks.

Warm pass: AoPipeline, WaterCopyPipeline, FogPipeline and LookPipeline are no longer exempt. The
exemption said a change of `gxMultisample` in the world compiles their shader live, but the world
camera reads it once at spawn, its target is always HDR and no booth carries `LookView`, so the
one variant each pass specialises on the camera's first frame, under the cover, is the only one.
`pipe_warm` now says so and names them.

World API wall, 131 to 121: ten crossings become methods on types already published, with the
same values and the same arithmetic. `WorldCamera::projection` and `zoomed_fovy` (CAM_FAR,
CAM_FOVY, NEARCLIP_DEFAULT), `ViewDistance::set_farclip` (FARCLIP_RANGE),
`MsaaSetting::in_range` (MSAA_RANGE), `RenderFade::self_body_alpha` (SELF_FADE_WINDOW,
self_model_fade_alpha), `WmoPortalInstance::down_ray_group` and `WorldPoint::interior_probe_eye`
(down_ray_seeds, terrain_z_local, INTERIOR_PROBE_HEIGHT).

Patch 0096 merged without a client-tests run and left two guards one over: Update's undeclared
pairs read 2,350 against 2,347 and its sync points 55 against 54, from the route lanterns'
chained `sync` and `apply`. Both ceilings follow the count, with the reason beside them.

Left alone: the rest of the schedule ceilings (PostUpdate 598, and the Update pairs above). They count undeclared-order
pairs, which a run condition does not change, and the pairs that remain are the effect drawers'
shared `EffectQuads` stream and `Transform` writers on disjoint lanes; declaring an order there
could change draw order.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
